rmation magic it is this magic  that allows him to turn into a fox and  of course when he turns himself into a  fox he becomes a much smaller target for  his opponents on top of that he has  incredible offensive capabilities both  with his arrows and with his bare hands  he is able to kill one of the talismans  on the spot with just a punch to the  abdomen for his part finish has a magic  called haste that gives him unbelievable  speed and in fact he can move so quickly  that purcell and the others can't even  follow his movements fidech tries to use  this speed to attack lancelot but  lancelot is able to dodge without even  breaking a sweat in fact lancelot  welcomes this battle as a nice little  warm-up because being a fox for a long  time makes him feel like his fighting  skills are out of practice no matter  what footage does and no matter how hard  he does it lancelot is able to  anticipate what he is doing and he  dodges and counters it before footage  can do anything it's almost as if  lancelot can anticipate viticus  movements before he even makes them but  more on that later lancelot then asks  fidech whether he knows a knight who has  a helmet with a star-shaped visor fidech  doesn't give a clear answer he just says  that he doesn't know what lancelot means  but even from that non-answer lancelot  is able to determine that fidech knows  the knight lancelot then asks a second  question does fittich know where dubs  the master craftsman of the giant clan  is this is of course the same dubs from  the cursed by light movie which gives  yet more credence to my argument that  the movie is canon once again even  though footage doesn't really answer  lancelot can tell that he doesn't know  where dubs is at this point finish  realizes that lancelot can somehow read  his mind which is why he was able to  anticipate all his movements before he  even made them so fidech just gives up  on the fight entirely and he attempts to  use his amazing speed to run away he  wants to get back to camelot and report  this monster called lancelot to king  arthur and the others fidech intends to  make lancelot one of the most wanted men  in britannia along with all the knights  of the apocalypse but lancelot just  calmly takes donny's dagger and uses a  spell called the shining road to turn  the dagger into some sort of homing  missile the dagger zooms through a  pathway of light until it catches up to  finish and destroys both him and his  horse in a matter of seconds damn  poor horse  as percival and the others look on in  shock our boy lancelot yeager simply  restates his previous statement anyone  who chooses to fight him will not live  to tell the tale back in camelot king  arthur learns that the dark talismans  have been destroyed as soon as it  happens because a talisman that he had  in his possession crumbles to pieces  when they die arthur casually says that  oh boy that was fast so maybe he should  take these so-called knights of the  apocalypse more seriously he asks merlin  if he should prioritize taking out the  four knights over finding a bride but  merlin just tells him to follow his own  wishes  bro who hurt this man not only did he go  and become a villain but he's out here  talking about finding a bride when he is  merlin right there arthur has completely  lost his damn mind and honestly i'm  getting more and more curious about what  happened to make arthur change so much  during the time skip between the  original series and the sequel the more  we learn about him and merlin the more  fascinating this question becomes  back in the entangled forest percival  and the gang are struggling to come to  terms with what an incredible badass  lancelot is and is shocked that he is  able to just kill the talismans without  batting an eye percival is crying and  thanking lancelot for saving them donnie  is upset that his dagger was broken and  nacienda is just like chilling i guess  when anne asks lancelot why he was going  around pretending to be a fox lancelot  explains that he is a servant of the  king of leonis and his mission is to  track down a potential member of the  four knights of the apocalypse and bring  him and his companions to leonis that is  exactly what he has been doing with  percival and the others his job was to  guide them to leonis while interfering  as little as possible i'm guessing that  this journey of theirs was also a sort  of test lancelot was observing percy in  order to determine whether he really was  one of the prophesized knights of the  apocalypse so because this was a type of  test he didn't want to just take them  all straight to leonis he wanted percy  to get stronger and prove himself during  the journey itself lancelot disguised  himself as a fox because he didn't want  the holy knights of camelot to discover  who he was and what he was doing but  lancelot was also the one looking out  for percy and the gang the whole time  like when he defeated all those demons  back in sistana and then said that his  friends did it  so it seems that lancelot serves as a  sort of secret agent for the king of  leonis and transformation magic is  basically the perfect magic for a secret  agent so lancelot is very good at his  job he carries out important secret  missions and he keeps such a low profile  that no one has ever heard of him before  and if they engage with him in battle  they don't live to tell about it and  unless something has changed in the last  few years we know that the king of  leonis is none other than meliodas so  that means that lancelot works directly  for meliodas himself this is extremely  cool because it means that we might  actually see meliodas in the story very  soon and i've been hoping for a long  time that the main characters from the  original story would start playing a  bigger role in the sequel so all of this  is a great sign as lancelot proceeds to  bury the dark talismans percy asks him  about the two people whom lancelot had  inquired abo